      "scenes": [
        {
          "id": "mh-s1",
          "start_ms": 0,
          "end_ms": 4711,
          "description": "Dusk on a Pune apartment balcony on Diwali: glowing akash kandil (star lantern), clay panti lamps on the ledge, rangoli at the doorway; the Aamod tin stands among the lamps.",
          "plate": "creative/mh_original/scenes/mh-s1_balcony.jpg",
          "on_screen_text_en": "Diwali means faral!",
          "image_model": "gemini-3.1-flash-image",
          "image_prompt": "A vertical 9:16 photograph at dusk on the balcony of an older apartment building in Pune, Maharashtra, on a Diwali evening. A large traditional akash kandil, a star-shaped paper lantern in saffron, red and yellow with paper tassels, hangs from the balcony ceiling and glows from inside. A row of small clay panti oil lamps burns along the balcony ledge. A colourful rangoli of dots and flower patterns decorates the balcony floor near the open doorway. Strings of warm lights; the neighbourhood's lit windows softly blurred in the background against a deep blue sky. On the ledge, among the lamps, stands the tin from the reference image, facing the camera. No people. Keep the upper third of the frame calm, mostly sky and soft lantern glow, for a headline. Keep the lower fifth of the frame simple."
        },
        {
          "id": "mh-s2",
          "start_ms": 4711,
          "end_ms": 10191,
          "description": "Grandmother (aaji) in a Paithani saree and her granddaughter arrange homemade faral (chakli, karanji, besan ladoo, shankarpali) on a brass plate; the tin on the table.",
          "plate": "creative/mh_original/scenes/mh-s2_aaji.jpg",
          "on_screen_text_en": "The taste of Grandma's cooking",
          "image_model": "gemini-3.1-flash-image",
          "image_prompt": "A vertical 9:16 photograph inside a warm Maharashtrian family home on Diwali. A grandmother in her late sixties, wearing a purple Paithani silk saree with a green and gold peacock border, and her granddaughter in her twenties, wearing a simple yellow festive kurta, sit at a wooden dining table, smiling and talking as they arrange homemade Diwali faral on a large round brass plate: spiral chakli, crescent-shaped karanji, round yellow besan ladoo and small diamond-shaped shankarpali. The closed tin from the reference image stands on the table next to the plate, facing the camera. Marigold garlands on the doorway behind them, clay diyas glowing on a shelf, soft evening window light. Candid, joyful, documentary-style family moment. Keep the upper quarter of the frame uncluttered (wall and garlands) for a headline."
        },
        {
          "id": "mh-s3",
          "start_ms": 10191,
          "end_ms": 15032,
          "description": "Product hero: the open Aamod tin filled with faral on a carved table with diyas and marigolds.",
          "plate": "creative/mh_original/scenes/mh-s3_tin.jpg",
          "on_screen_text_en": "Faral that tastes like home, now in one tin",
          "image_model": "gemini-3.1-flash-image",
          "image_prompt": "A vertical 9:16 close-up food photograph. The tin from the reference image stands on a carved wooden table, its brass-gold lid leaning against its side, filled to the top with Maharashtrian Diwali faral: spiral chakli, crescent-shaped karanji, round besan ladoo and diamond-shaped shankarpali. The tin's front with the round cream medallion faces the camera. Around it: small glowing clay diyas, a few marigold flowers and petals, a red and gold cloth, warm bokeh lights in the background. Appetising, premium, warm golden light. The tin is the hero, placed in the lower middle of the frame; keep the upper third calm and dark for a headline."
        },
        {
          "id": "mh-s4",
          "start_ms": 15032,
          "end_ms": 19912,
          "description": "Bhau Beej: the sister (the granddaughter from scene 2) performs aukshan (aarti) for her brother seated on a pat; he gives her the Aamod tin.",
          "plate": "creative/mh_original/scenes/mh-s4_bhaubeej.jpg",
          "on_screen_text_en": "Give a sweet gift this Bhau Beej",
          "image_model": "gemini-3.1-flash-image",
          "image_prompt": "A vertical 9:16 photograph of a Bhau Beej celebration in a Maharashtrian home: two siblings close in age. The sister, a young woman of about twenty-two, is the young woman shown in the second reference image (same face, hair and features); she is not middle-aged. She wears a green festive silk saree and holds a brass aarti plate with a small lit diya, rice and kumkum, performing the aukshan ritual for her brother, a young man of about eighteen. He sits cross-legged on a low wooden pat with a colourful rangoli in front of it, wearing a cream kurta, and with both hands he presents her the tin from the first reference image. Both are laughing warmly. Warm diya light, marigold garlands, a softly lit home in the background. Keep the upper quarter of the frame uncluttered for a headline."
        },
        {
